      "source": "gate:pr_scope_judgment",
      "source_status": "needs_split",
      "summary": "Keep story-vibepro-symlinked-bin-entrypoint as one PR rather than the suggested 3-lane split",
      "reason": "The two commits on this branch are a single coherent bug fix (realpath-based direct-execution predicate for symlinked bin/vibepro.js invocation) plus its own Story/Spec/Architecture SSOT docs and design-ssot lineage links, and a second process-only commit declaring the Story-local review dispatch budget in .vibepro/config.json. The split-plan's suggested requirements-ssot/runtime-behavior/repo-control lanes are all one indivisible change: the doc trio exists only to describe this exact fix, the test file only exercises this exact fix, and the budget commit only exists to let this Story's own review dispatches proceed. Splitting would force reviewers to read the Story/Spec/Architecture docs in one PR with no code to check them against, and the code fix in another PR with no accepted rationale. No other work item's history got bundled in; this is solely a revival/rebase of PR #361 onto current origin/main.",
